-- title:
--   All q-coefficients of a normalized eigenform are algebraic integers
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number, and assume the hypothesis [`CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L6), namely that the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by those cusp forms all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients [`ModularFormClass.qCoeff`](def/FLTPrelim_Modularity.html#L19) lie in the image of $\mathbb{Z}$ is the whole space. Let $f$ be a cusp form of weight $2$ for $\Gamma_0(N)$ satisfying the project predicate [`CuspForm.IsNormalizedEigenform`](def/FLTPrelim_Modularity.html#L28), i.e. its $q$-coefficients $a_n =$ `qCoeff f n` satisfy: $a_1 = 1$; $a_{mn} = a_m a_n$ whenever $m$ and $n$ are coprime; for every prime $p$ not dividing $N$ and every $r$, $a_{p^{r+2}} = a_p a_{p^{r+1}} - p\,a_{p^r}$; and for every prime $p$ dividing $N$ and every $r$, $a_{p^{r+2}} = a_p a_{p^{r+1}}$. Then for every natural number $n$ there exists an element $a$ of the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}$ in $\mathbb{C}$ whose image in $\mathbb{C}$ equals $a_n$; that is, every Fourier coefficient of $f$ is an algebraic integer.
--
--   This is the standard integrality statement for the Fourier coefficients of a normalized Hecke eigenform of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(N)$, here deduced from the corresponding statement at primes. It feeds the construction of the $\ell$-adic Galois representation attached to $f$, where the characteristic polynomials of Frobenius elements are expressed through these coefficients.
